  "verification_scope": "GFG pp3–7 visually inspected; both reproductions OCR reviewed throughout, with targeted visual checks GateForum pp5,8,10,14. This is a structural inventory and material-variant audit, not a full symbol-by-symbol equivalence certification. Physical PDF page references may include shared stem pages. No third-party solutions copied or authored.",
  "discrepancies": [
    {
      "question": "scope",
      "note": "Both reproductions cover original A groups 1–8 and B groups 9–28, including substantial descriptive material. This is observed reproduction coverage only, not certification of the original paper. GFG last label 50 hides grouped 2/3 and unnumbered original15."
    },
    {
      "question": "1.20",
      "note": "GFG p3 options (c)/(d) are array / array element; GateForum p4 swaps these and corrupts final option text. Use semantic answer rather than transplanting a letter."
    },
    {
      "question": "1.21",
      "note": "GFG p3 option (c) loses words after longer than the; GateForum p4 says longer than the address space of a computer. Do not silently conflate address space with physical memory."
    },
    {
      "question": "1.23",
      "note": "GFG p3 option (c) appears to read g2(n) is O(g2(n)), while GateForum p4 reads O(g1(n)); needs careful source-specific handling rather than assuming common options."
    },
    {
      "question": "1.24",
      "note": "GateForum p5 option (c) omits NOT before first fit; GFG p3 has best fit but not first fit. Diagram labels are segment lengths, not inferred boundary addresses."
    },
    {
      "question": "2.6",
      "note": "GateForum p5 explicitly gives P(B)=P1, P(A intersect B)=P2, P(A intersect complement B)=P3. GFG p3 is corrupted, repeats P2 and omits part of the prompt. Use GateForum text with provenance disclosure."
    },
    {
      "question": "3.7",
      "note": "GFG p4 omits the question Can you conclude; GateForum p7 retains it. Distinct values in one instance are the given condition, not an asserted schema key."
    },
    {
      "question": "4",
      "note": "Complement bars in the Boolean operator and equation must be read from rasters. They are lost in OCR; no formula should be reconstructed from plain extraction alone."
    },
    {
      "question": "5",
      "note": "GateForum p8 prints 2(n−1)+3; GFG28 p5 omits +3 and prints 2(n−1). The source formulas differ materially."
    },
    {
      "question": "9",
      "note": "Neither stem explicitly identifies even versus odd parity for the Hamming code. Preserve any parity convention used; inspect the received bits in the figure, not OCR."
    },
    {
      "question": "13(a)",
      "note": "GateForum p10 asks for students who HAVE registered for cno322; GFG36 p6 asks HAVE NOT registered. These are opposite query variants."
    },
    {
      "question": "14(a)",
      "note": "GateForum p10 omits the key to insert; GFG37 p6 explicitly says insert100. Both require visual reading of the B+ tree, not OCR labels."
    },
    {
      "question": "15",
      "note": "GFG p6 suppresses the original question number and part(a) label, running the summation proofs immediately after original14(b). GateForum p11 labels them15(a)/(b). Both must be counted separately from14."
    },
    {
      "question": "16",
      "note": "GFG38 p6 loses equality in a o a = a; GateForum16 p11 retains the idempotence equation."
    },
    {
      "question": "19(a)",
      "note": "This is a four-option choice embedded within a descriptive Section B group, retained as one MCQ leaf. It does not belong to the initial24 MCQs."
    },
    {
      "question": "20",
      "note": "GateForum p12 omits the symbol after length; GFG42 p6 prints length l. Preserve variable l, not a numeric1 inferred from OCR."
    },
    {
      "question": "27",
      "note": "Both code reproductions show no loop-back jump between increment and next label. Do not silently insert a loop. GateForum p13 also loses the next label that GFG49 p7 retains."
